# 17. Print only matching lines, like grep. Pement: sed -n '/regexp/p'
# -n (the #ARGS line) switches off the automatic print at the end of every
# cycle, so only lines that reach the p command appear. The equivalent
# without -n is  sed '/regexp/!d'. For grep -v use  /regexp/d  (or -n with !p).
# Try: change the #ARGS line to  #ARGS  (nothing) and every line prints, the
#      matches twice.
#ARGS -n
/an/p

